I don't want to be too spoily but I mildly disagree.
In the case of the OP, who is new to the game, I would say a wand of
digging deserves a lot more than just an 'honorable mention'.  As long
as you are not blind, confused, etc. it works every time in just 1
turn.  I go through games where I never see an athame but see plenty of
wands of digging and only a few wands of fire/lightning.  Wands of
digging are more common than F/L and in the early game one needs to
make the best use of what they can find.

Save the wands of F/L for when you want to melee while standing on
Elbereth, and use wands of digging or dust for when your pets can
handle the fighting or you are willing to risk rubbing out your
engraving.



